// A union `==` between two values with a literal-union alias arm beside a scalar arm compares
// the alias arm as its member string (D5260), at a binding, a parameter, a call operand, a list
// element, a declared alias, a nullable spelling and an `f64` arm.
type K = "x" | "y"
type KI = K | i32
const a: K | i32 = "x"
const b: K | i32 = "x"
const c: K | i32 = 3
const d: K | i32 = "y"
print(a == b)
print(a == c)
print(a == d)
print(c == c)
print(a != b)
function eq(p: K | i32, q: K | i32): boolean { p == q }
print(eq("x", "x"))
print(eq("x", "y"))
function g(n: i32): K | i32 {
  if n > 0 { return "x" }
  n
}
print(g(1) == a)
print(g(0) == a)
const xs: KI[] = ["x", 3]
const ys: KI[] = ["x", 4]
print(xs[0] == ys[0])
print(xs[1] == ys[1])
const na: K | i32 | null = "x"
const nb: K | i32 | null = "x"
const nn: K | i32 | null = null
print(na == nb)
print(na == nn)
print(nn == nn)
const fa: K | f64 = "y"
const fb: K | f64 = 1.5
const fc: K | f64 = 1.5
print(fb == fc)
print(fa == fb)
print(fa == fa)
print(eq(3, 4))
print(eq(3, "x"))
